Negative control  --  the old pursuit heuristic must disagree where it is known wrong
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   On the RETAINED segments the heuristic agrees with barrier.py 98.7% of the time,
   against grad V's 98.7%. The two are indistinguishable there, and that is a fact
   about the scope, not about the laws: scoping A-C to the retained segments keeps
   only short range (max retained R = 6.26), and the heuristic is known to track the
   paper at short range and invert beyond R ~ 8. So the control has to be run where
   it is meant to discriminate: against the grid law over the whole domain.

   grid law vs heuristic, disagreement by range band:
      0.5 -  2.0     9.68% of nodes
      2.0 -  4.0    10.40% of nodes
      4.0 -  6.0    29.05% of nodes
      6.0 -  8.0    41.97% of nodes
      8.0 - 10.0    48.01% of nodes
     10.0 - 12.0    50.70% of nodes
  PASS  the heuristic diverges from the grid law as range grows   monotone from 9.7% to 50.7%
  PASS  beyond R = 8 the heuristic is near a coin flip against the correct law   disagreement 48.0% to 50.7%

